    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1449">

                <pb facs="1222" n="1118" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/14.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 493,
                    of the 4th instant, reporting on the subject of the recent Panaman legislation
                    affecting the immigration and residence of Chinese in Panama.</p>
                <p>A copy of your despatch has been forwarded to the American Legation at Peking for
                    its information in connection with previous <pb facs="1223" n="1119"
                        xml:id="pg1119"/> telegraphic correspondence between the Department and the
                    Legation on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
